                <pb facs="0113" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg23"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1769: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-25T12:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 6:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>227. Department’s telegram 167, September 23rd, 4 p.m. Request for additional
                    marines Camaguey based on necessity for protection sugar interest owned by
                    Americans in four eastern provinces. It is estimated that a considerable
                    percentage of total sugar production of 1920 crop controlled by American
                    interests. English, Spanish and other foreign interests are also important. It
                    is openly stated by partisans of both parties that in event of revolution or
                    other disturbances American interests will be first to be destroyed.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
